Z||000000||Formula||11-20-2000||09:48 PM||||anyone know how I could go about this?  I want to give it a shot and I was thinking about the following ingredients.....<P>either a wood, plexiglass, or fiberglass base<P>the wood would be easy, but might be ugly, and might rot or be heavy.... If I went with wood could I cover it in aluminum foil/tin and make it look like it is silver/chrome?<BR>maybe put mirrors on it?<P>plexiglass would be a little bit harder but might be too brittle.  it would be neat to have it clear so that you could see into the front of the car some.  <P>I have no idea how to make a fiberglass mold so this is pretty much out.  <P>I want to go with projection style lights that are round.  probably blue low beams and white high beams, and have low beams as day time running lamps, and replace my fog lights with super high output lights to make up for any lost light.  how would I wire these?  how could I mount them.<P>I want to make a plexiglass cover for them and possibly tint it.  would I just have to cut out the glass and go from there?<BR>does tint stay on plexiglass?<P>I want some of your ideas on cool headlight mods too.  I was going to buy this mod but I figured I did everything else myself so I mine as well take on this challenge.<P>PLEASE make a sugestion, and if you know an answer, PLEASE describe how to do this, I would ask TOM but he seems to have low internet access now.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FormulaSignature2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
