Z||000005||rogergarrison||11-21-2000||07:51 PM||||thats exactly what im doing for my winter project. Ive bought 96 camaro headlites and buckets with adjusters. Im taking out the complete stock assembly and bolting the new low profile buckets on the bulkhead. Their only about 2 1/2 inches high. then im going to frame the opening with extruded aluminum to have a mounting surface for the clear Lexan covers mounted flush with hood. im going to finish out the open space inside with sheet metal painted flat black. I wouldnt suggest tinting it, the sharp angle is going to cut some of the lite anyway, and tinting may make your lites too dim. A plastic supplier can usually cut and finish the edges for you if you provide them with an exact pattern for a charge. Dont use plexiglas by the way, use Lexan, will bend and take more stone impact without breaking. Ill have mine finished before winter is over. <P>no more sticking doors, or goofy lites popping up like bug eyes, lol  ||||reg||1
